t turns the whole legend into blocks at full scale. Each legend cell becomes a square of the block size. Neighbouring blocks sit one *step* apart, and the step is the x-distance between the existing blocks: 5 in pairs 1 and 3, 3 in pair 2. The same step is used vertically. Legend cells that are background stay empty.\n\n**How the legend is anchored.** The existing blocks are a copy of part of the legend:\n\n- Pair 1: the blocks are 4,4, which is legend row 0.\n- Pair 2: the blocks are 2,2, which is legend row 0. The legend there has a third column (3 in rows 2–3), and it is drawn one step to the right.\n- Pair 3: the blocks are 3,4, which is legend row 2. So the new rows are drawn *above* the existing blocks.\n\nSo I look for the place (r, c) in the legend matrix where the block colours appear left to right. That place fixes where legend cell (0,0) lands: `y0 - r*step`, `x0 - c*step`. Every non-background legend cell is then stamped as a block. Blocks that run past the canvas edge are clipped.\n\n**Test.** The legend is\n- 1 1 1\n- 4 4 2\n- 1 4 1\n- 8 . .\n\nThe blocks are 4,2 (size 4, step 5). They match row 1, columns 1–2. So column 0 falls at x=8 and row 0 at y=5. Row 3's 8-block starts at y=25 and is clipped at the bottom edge.\n\n**Teaching stages.** The program emits one canvas per legend row drawn, then the final canvas.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    singles = [o for o in objs if o[\"size\"] == 1]\n    blocks = sorted([o for o in objs if o[\"size\"] > 1], key=lambda o: o[\"box\"][1])\n    ys = sorted(set(o[\"box\"][0] for o in singles))\n    xs = sorted(set(o[\"box\"][1] for o in singles))\n    L = np.full((len(ys), len(xs)), bg)\n    for o in singles:\n        L[ys.index(o[\"box\"][0]), xs.index(o[\"box\"][1])] = o[\"colour\"]\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = blocks[0][\"box\"]\n    size = y1 - y0 + 1\n    step = blocks[1][\"box\"][1] - x0 if len(blocks) > 1 else size + 1\n    cols = [b[\"colour\"] for b in blocks]\n    R, C = L.shape\n    found = None\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C - len(cols) + 1):\n            if all(L[r, c + i] == cols[i] for i in range(len(cols))):\n                found = (r, c)\n                break\n        if found:\n            break\n    r0, c0 = found\n    oy, ox = y0 - r0 * step, x0 - c0 * step\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = out.shape\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            if L[r, c] == bg:\n                continue\n            ty, tx = oy + r * step, ox + c * step\n            ya, yb = max(ty, 0), min(ty + size, H)\n            xa, xb = max(tx, 0), min(tx + size, W)\n            if ya < yb and xa < xb:\n                out[ya:yb, xa:xb] = L[r, c]\n        emit(out, f\"Stamped legend row {r} as {size}x{size} blocks at step {step}.\")\n    emit(out, \"All legend cells drawn at full scale, aligned to the existing blocks.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"legend":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **A legend** in the top-left corner."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What the output adds.** The output turns the whole legend into blocks at full scale."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each legend cell becomes a square of the block size."}],"movement":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"All legend cells drawn at full scale, aligned to the existing blocks."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Every non-background legend cell is then stamped as a block."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamped legend row 0 as 3x3 blocks at step 5."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamped legend row 1 as 3x3 blocks at step 5."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"So column 0 falls at x=8 and row 0 at y=5."}],"scale":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What the output adds.** The output turns the whole legend into blocks at full scale."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"All legend cells drawn at full scale, aligned to the existing blocks."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"04c81e1e112d011df4b4dcf104a6b1e8a220ea815810c5d65af6df33ca173df8","task_sha256":"93fc4e7c5e29544a1416e345b3576e2696c20c84a9036ced05aca4bb5393ab6e","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
